usrd: Can I use the 'SELECT ... LIMIT' statement in my Vue.js server-side code?
Answer

Yes, you can use the 'SELECT ... LIMIT' SQL statement in Vue.js server-side code. Vue.js uses a library called vue-query to communicate with the database. Here is an example:

```javascript
import * as query from 'vue-query';

// define your model
// ...

Vue.use(query)

const postQuery = {
  models: ['posts'],
  where: { title: { $like: /hello/ } }
};

query({ postQuery })
  .then(({ data }) => {
    console.log(data.posts);
  })
  .catch((err) => {
    console.error(err);
  });
```

In the example above, `vue-query` will send a SELECT query to the database with a condition on the `title` field like '/hello/'. It then awaits the response from the database and logs the returned data posts array. If there was an error, it would log the error message. 

Please replace `['posts']` and `{ title: { $like: /hello/ } }` with your actual model names and condition respectively. Also make sure your data source in Vue.js is properly connected to your database. 

Keep in mind that it's important to sanitize user inputs in SQL queries to prevent SQL Injection attacks.
